The reason Shaula remained in the tower was “his” order, but among the companions starting with Mama-sama―― “Reilani” was also supposed to have been one of them. Despite that, being told something like “It must have been lonely” as if it were someone else's problem ticked her off.
The sense of duty to protect “his” order was burning brightly inside Shaula. Having water thrown on that with sentimental feelings like being lonely was truly detestable.

Shaula: [Actually, leaving aside whether I'm lonely or not~,]

Reilani: […Well then, were you not lonely?]

Shaula: [Like I wa~aas! This conversation is over~! I mean, what about you guys~. All your buddies got completely wiped out, and you ended up returning empty-handed, so what did you even come to the tower for~?]

The part about not bringing “him” along was the biggest flaw from Shaula's perspective, but to begin with, there was no doubt that Reilani's objective was this tower.

Shaula: [Anyway, outside this stupidly wide Sand Sea, there's absolutely nothing other than this tower~.]

As far as the eye could see, a sand-colored world where nothing could be found―― that was the space that had enveloped Shaula for hundreds of years, and the place she would continue to spend her time in while waiting for “his” return. She was a little curious as to why “Reilani”, who had returned as a distraction, had come back.
Perhaps――,

Shaula: [――Master,]

Had he sent “Reilani” here to bring her along, she thought.
Of course, even if “Reilani” were to say so, Shaula would not comply with that. To the bitter end, Shaula would strictly observe the words of “him” who told her to wait for him here. ――However, she could feel love in the fact that “he” was caring about her.
If she had that, she felt like the hundreds of years up until now, and the hundreds of years from now on, would be rewarded.
However――,

Reilani: [――I am deeply sorry. Powerless me has no answer that can meet your expectations.]

Shaula: [――――]

With the answer of Reilani, who bowed her head deeply as she said so, Shaula briefly held her breath.
Well, that figured. Things were not that convenient. Things going exactly as Shaula expected wouldn't happen that easily. She had fully understood that.
Because it was something she fully understood, there was no way she could be hurt.

Shaula: [A~ah, I was a huge idiot for getting my hopes up~. I'm disappointed in you from the bottom of my heart~.]

Slowly shaking her head from side to side, Shaula kicked away a small pebble that was rolling on the stone floor.
It was strange. Why were there small pebbles rolling around on the floor of the fourth floor, which was in such a high place? It wasn't at a height where they would be carried by the wind either. Who had brought these here, and how?
Her nerves were frayed to the point where she was bothered by such trivial things.

Shaula: [Even if you don't prepare meals or anything on your own~. Because of me taking care of you, it can't be helped up to this point~.]

Shaula: [Even if that's not the case, there's no way you can endure the meals I prepared for you~. What you can eat here is about the level of the Witchbeasts living in the Sand Sea, and those taste like rotten ditch water anyway.]

Shaula: [At best, it's best you use your own food to give nourishment to the baby in your belly. Go walking outside on your own volition~. I'm making the rules around here now~.]

Strictly speaking, “he” who had imposed the rules on Shaula was the rule himself, but she had no intention of telling Reilani that. She hated it.
Why should she give what the other person wanted to an opponent who wouldn't give Shaula what she wanted.

2

Farsale: [――What's wrong, Shaula? Making such a longing face. Alright, my eminent self shall share some of my steamed potato with you.]

Laughing like that, a person with golden hair and red eyes split the steamed potato in their hands into two. Then, comparing the split potatoes, they offered the larger one to Shaula with an “Nn”.
Shaula thought it was a carefree, giddy smile. Having thought that, while receiving the potato, she tilted her head at the way of thinking of the other party―― the blonde hair, who handed her the larger of the two potatoes.

Shaula: [Agh, isn't Farsale's way of thinking a little bit hard to understand?~. Why would you give the bigger one to me~? Is it a life hack to suck up to the strong ones to survive~?]

Farsale: [Do not be foolish. If that were the correct way of thinking, the one my eminent self should be offering the potato to would be Reid, or Volcanica. Besides, if it were those two, half a potato would not suffice. I believe so. To think they are utterly hopeless in terms of humanity. Dost thou not think so?]

As soon as she pictured those two in her mind, Shaula's lips twisted grandly. Seeing that reaction, the blonde hair laughed as if having gotten exactly what he wanted, and patted the spot right next to himself with his hand. Having no reason to refuse the blonde hair's invitation to sit, Shaula effortlessly sat down.
Dangling her legs at the edge of the cliff where they sat, Shaula nibbled on the still-hot potato. For a while, a time of silently nibbling on potatoes continued between Shaula and the blonde hair.

Shaula: [――――]

A large, large red sunset was sinking behind the mountains opposite them. In a little while, night would arrive, and that darkness would likely bring a dazzling starry sky. For Shaula, who had good night vision, the darkness of the night was nothing to sneeze at. Therefore, she just couldn't wait for the night that brought the starry sky.

Farsale: [Shaula, art thou not cold?]

Suddenly, the blonde hair, who had also finished eating his potato, asked Shaula as she licked the fingers that had finished eating her potato. Shaula, who had her shoulders, belly, and legs exposed, snorted at that question,

Shaula: [Cold~? I haven't felt that at all~. Are we sharing the common delusion of weaklings~?]

Farsale: [So the coldness my eminent self is feeling is an illusion! That is an interesting way of thinking. However, the wind is feeling cold, whether it is an illusion or not. Draw closer, for my eminent self's sake.]

Shaula: [Sh-can't be helped then~]

Opening the white cloak he had draped over himself, Shaula shrugged her shoulders at the blonde hair who said so, and moved her butt by half a cheek, and then another half a cheek, drawing close enough to a position where the other party could embrace her shoulders. Slipping smoothly into the cloak's...

...inside, receiving Shaula's weight as she settled in, the blonde hair nodded with an “Umu”.

Farsale: [As expected, human skin is warm. Even you have body heat. Is it that you do not feel the cold?]

Shaula: [Tsk, tsk, tsk, such weak elements have been completely eliminated from my Star-keeper machine fully spec'd for protecting Master, which is what I am~. Don't go fitting me into such weak common sense~.]

Farsale: [Mu, is that so. That is quite shallow of my eminent self. However…]

Shaula: [――? What is it~?]

Farsale: [For my eminent self, I do not think that snuggling up to someone is a condition of weakness. I consider it a good thing, and I have a mindset that thinks highly of Lady 'Witch'.]

As he spoke, the blonde hair pulled Shaula's body in closer, as if to reinforce his own theory. She didn't go out of her way to shake it off, and it was a fact that Mama-sama had problems with her humanity, but there was something about the blonde hair's opinion that made it difficult to nod honestly.

Shaula: [No matter what Farsale says, my priority of Master being number one is absolute~! Any factor that could disrupt that order is an instant BAD-BAN for me~! Aren't all of Master's companions just people with broken humanity?]

Farsale: [You have a habit of asking questions with double meanings! …Truly, a difficult question]

The first half was answered like the usual blonde, while the second half was answered unlike him. Such a subtle nuance difference up to the fine details put into it, Shaula could not fully pick up on. It was Shaula's way of thinking that she didn't even want to pick up on it. If she let Mama-sama say it, this too was a necessary function so as not to connect it to weakness.

Shaula: [Whatever~, I just think humans are all such a hassle~.]

Farsale: […I cannot deny that, but is it fine? Your beloved Master is also a human.]

Shaula: [Master is literally a special existence, so he can't even be placed on the same line as other humans in the first place~! So, no prob~! No-paso~!]

Farsale: [I know not what 'no-paso' means yet... I must ask him its meaning later. Still, to be able to state so clearly that he is special—thou art remarkable. So strong.]

The smiling blonde hair patted her head. She hated having her precious scorpion tail messed up, but the profile she looked up at looked dejected, so she didn't brush his hand away.

Shaula: [Strong, huh. You are]

With his dejected face, the blonde hair continued to pat Shaula's head and muttered.
Even Shaula understood that the nuance imbued in that mutter wasn't simply just envying her. It was also not a mistake that the blonde hair's red eyes were wet.
What the blonde hair envied was probably not Shaula's strength. ――It was thinking of someone special, and proudly speaking of it. That was what he felt envious of.

Shaula: […Humans sure are a pain~.]

Why the blonde hair envied her, Shaula didn't understand the fine details.

The blonde hair was a royal or something, a position where he originally had to be in a castle. He had a foolishly bright and completely fearless personality, and often got caught up in trouble. In terms of strength, he was completely lacking, and leaving the resolution of the trouble he caused to others―― in the aspect of borrowing the strength of others, he might share something with “him”. Though “he” was a hundred times cooler.

However, when she wanted to brag about “him” to someone, for Shaula who couldn't tell “him” himself, the blonde hair was a precious conversation partner. The blonde hair, who would give fresh, flashy, and big reactions to any story, could truly be called the ideal person to brag to.

To speak frankly, the blonde hair, drawing close like this and sharing warmth, was for Shaula――,

Farsale: [――It is night, huh.]

Suddenly, at the voice that sounded like it was whispering in her ear, Shaula realized the arrival of night belatedly.

Understanding that her consciousness had been so directed towards the blonde hair's state that she hadn't even noticed the arrival of the night she had been eagerly awaiting, Shaula somehow felt a restless mood.

The various large and small white points of light scattered across the curtain of night―― twinkling as if their existence there was only natural, she had heard Mama-sama speak wisely that all of them were massive and mighty clumps of mana beyond human comprehension. But, Shaula had a different view on the light of the stars.

This was also something she was repeating that she had been taught by “him”, and for that very reason, it was an absolute fact within Shaula.

Shaula: [――What the stars are, are the crystallization of the wishes of a whole bunch of people~.]

Farsale: [Shaula?]

She could tell that the blonde hair's eyes widened blankly at Shaula who suddenly started talking. But, Shaula did not look up at the face of the person right next to her. She just continued while looking at the starry sky.

Shaula: [Every time you look up at the sky, some guy is entrusting a wish to the sky~. When that accumulates, and gathers up, it shines brightly and becomes a star. So, occasionally, that shining star grants someone's wish~.]

Farsale: […Whose wish, is it. Under what conditions is it chosen?]

Shaula: [That's totally random~!]

Farsale: [What! It is not the one who worked the hardest!]

Shaula: [Since they're stars, they don't have free time, so they don't look all the way to see who worked the hardest or desperately made a wish~. Even if they grant a wish after much trouble, there's no way they're gonna play favorites. So, it's a random, serious gamble~.]

Gripping her fist tightly, Shaula emphasized this, and the blonde hair's shoulders shook with a “Kuku”. It seemed he was somewhat distracted. Having distracted him, Shaula would say this as well.

Shaula: [And, since I'm the Star-keeper, I'm the girl of the constellation bearing the name of the stars. It's almost like giving me the same role as the stars, so taking advice from me wouldn't be overkill~.]

Farsale: [Advice, you say? That is, for having a wish granted by the stars, I presume. But if it is true that the stars choose the wishes to grant randomly…]

Shaula: [But, to somewhat attract that randomness, the life hack to get fate on your side is and, I completely messed up~! I ended up saying fate~!]

While she was getting carried away talking, she had unintentionally blurted out fatalism and such. That invisible force called “fate” was greatly hated by Shaula's precious “him”.
That was why she was being careful not to carelessly say things like she was his destined woman, and yet.

Shaula: [Guh, what a blunder~… If it's come to this, I'll just have the stars grant my wish to make it so that my slip of the tongue just now never happened~…!]

Farsale: [Wait, wait, wait! Were you not just about to teach my eminent self that method!? What is to become of my eminent self's warm and fuzzy feelings!?]

Shaula: [In the end, life is just the survival of the fittest, and everything is just a game of musical chairs~…]

Farsale: [Is that alright!? Is it truly alright for the conclusion up to this point to be that!?]

Shaula: [Is the right to have your own wish granted that important~? It's a huge turn-off~…]

Farsale: [It is something that happens rather often, but this is the most innovative pulling of the ladder out from under someone in a while!]

Covering her ears at the blonde hair who was becoming yappy and noisy as usual, Shaula felt like she genuinely didn't need to give any more advice.
That being said, having the blonde hair close in on her like this and endlessly nagging her would be troublesome, so Shaula revealed her prized secret with a “Good grief~”.
The method to win the rights of the stars, that was――,

Shaula: [――It's to shine so brightly that even the stars in the night sky would be captivated by you~.]

3

Shaula: [――I did say to shine brightly, though~.]

It didn't sit right with her at all. ――With such feelings in her chest, Shaula was in a sulky mood.
Beyond her vision, at a place called a court banquet where a large number of humans were mingling, the blonde hair, clad in a dazzling outfit and adorned all over with numerous pieces of jewelry, was surrounded by people.

Because he was what was called “royalty”, it was only natural for him to be pampered by his surroundings. Besides, no matter where he was, the blonde hair was always cheerful and seemed to be having fun, unchanging.

That being said, the "brightly" Shaula spoke of wasn't about wearing a bunch of jangling precious metals, but did the blonde hair understand that?

Shaula: [If he doesn't understand it, then that's the gift of thought suspension~. Humans are thinking reed… I don't know what a reed is~, but he ain't a reed like that~.]

Alec: [What's this, what's this. Could it be that you're in a bad mood, Shaula-kun?]

Shaula: [Oh, wondering who it was, the beard has arrived~.]

As she looked at the banquet and the blonde hair in the center of it from a distance, a bearded man with dark brown hair came over with a face like he had found a left-out companion. That beard, with a cane in one hand, lined up next to Shaula with a walking style as if dragging one leg,

Alec: [There is no mistaking that I have grown a beard, but I am not happy being called that. I have the name Alec. Lately, I've been trying to add Hoshin to it, too.]

Shaula: [Ah~! Come to think of it, I heard about that~! Ain't that the name you got from Master or something~! What's the big idea~, you wanna go at it with me~?]

Alec: [I won't do it. Even if we did, it would be so one-sided that even you would get sick of it.]

Saying so with a wry smile, the beard supported his body with his cane and lifted one leg to show her. It was a crippled leg due to some old injury or something. In short, he probably wanted to say that he couldn't move satisfactorily because of it.

Shaula: [If you start saying you can't move satisfactorily, Mama-sama would be pitiful~. Even though Mama-sama isn't hurt anywhere at all, she sprains both her ankles just by walking~.]

Alec: [Lady 'Witch' is a problem in a different sense than I am, as Lady 'Witch'. To make up for that, since you are energetic and sturdy, Lady 'Witch' must be proud of you as well.]

Shaula: [Whoops, even if you flatter me like that, the suspicion of the beard sneaking up to Master hasn't disappeared~. In the end, what happened with the name thing~. Did you seduce my Master~? Where? With what? How~?]

Alec: [Even if you close in on me with such deep interest, I only had a fun conversation with your Master.]

Shifting her interest from the banquet to the beard, Shaula pressed the other party aggressively. Deepening his wry smile at Shaula, who glared up at him from below like that, the beard shrugged his shoulders easily,

Alec: [It is true that I got the inspiration for the name from your Master, but you can rest assured. It's not like I borrowed the name of a star. The auspicious name your Master knows… a synonym for success in life, I had him allow me to borrow such a name.]

Shaula: [Success in liiiife?]

Alec: [It means to establish oneself and succeed through one's work. Originally, that was the number one reason I left my hometown. Even if the world gets a little shaky, I cannot compromise on that.]

Shaula: [Hoe~, so you're riding on Master's jinx~. I totally thought the beard was more of a realist pessimist~, but you're a romantic, huh~.]

Alec: [I don't know what you thought of me, and in the end, I don't know what you think of me now either, if you say that.]

Shaula: [――――]

At the strange tone of voice thrown in the middle of their exchange, Shaula's eyes went wide. Seeming pleased with Shaula's reaction, the beard winked playfully.
Feeling like she had been bested by that, to cover up her dissatisfaction, Shaula considered snapping the beard's precious cane in half, but――,

Alec: [――Shaula-kun, it seems you've been nominated.]

Staring fixedly at the cane, Shaula raised her face with a “Fwaa?” at the beard's call. Then, at the end of the beard's pointing chin, she caught sight of the blonde hair slipping out of the lively group at the banquet and bustling over towards Shaula and the others.
With that momentum, the blonde hair grabbed Shaula's hand, glanced at the beard beside her,

Farsale: [Eei, my eminent self is at his limit any further! Alec, I leave the rest to you!]

Alec: [Yeah, understood. ――Shaula-kun, take care of Farsale-kun.]

Shaula: [Haa~? I don't know what's going on~, don't pull me~hk!]

Without being able to read the flow, Shaula was led by the blonde hair pulling her arm, slipping out of the venue. Behind them, she could tell that the beard, quickly stepping in, was stopping the crowd that wanted to talk to the blonde hair.
The beard struck the floor strongly with his cane, drawing the attention of the place to himself, and,

Alec: [Ladies and gentlemen, please wait a moment. If you chase after him with such momentum, His Highness will be in a great panic. For now, it would be better to listen to my story here.]

And with that, using the mysterious tone that had perplexed Shaula earlier, he had succeeded in stopping the group.
In any case――,

Farsale: [Phew! Finally, I can relax my shoulders.]

Slipping out of the banquet venue and arriving at a gazebo standing alone in the garden where the night breeze blew, the blonde hair said so while stretching out grandly. Forced to accompany that stretch because her arm was grabbed, Shaula looked at him with half-closed eyes,

Shaula: [Was it alright for you to slip out~? All those swarming guys, ee~everyone wanted to talk to you, y'know~?]

Farsale: [When you say it like that my eminent self's chest hurts as well, but if my eminent self does not have time to take a breather, my eminent self will suffocate! …Of course, I am aware that whining over something of this level is nothing to be praised for.]

Shaula: [I'm not particularly blaming you~. What you do is your freedom~.]

Farsale: [“My freedom”, is it...?]

Her grabbed hand being released, Shaula lowered her arm and looked suspiciously at the blonde hair's reaction.
The blonde hair usually had a foolishly bright face, but at the banquet, that open and frank atmosphere was fully unleashed even more. And yet now, the blonde hair in front of Shaula only slightly lowered the corners of his eyes and relaxed his lips, looking much less foolish.

Shaula: [When you're like that, you don't look like an idiot~.]

Farsale: [Is that so… hm? An idiot!? Did you just call my eminent self an idiot!?]

Shaula: [I didn't say it~. I said that unlike usual, you don't look like one right now~.]

Farsale: [In other words, does that not mean you always think my eminent self is an idiot!? Does it not!?]

Shaula: [Not just usually, but you're back to being an idiot now too~!]

At Shaula's impression, which lacked any particular ill intent, the blonde hair swept his own hair up with both hands, groaning "Uu" and "Aa" for a while, but soon nodded with an "Umu",

Farsale: [Very well. Given the relationship between my eminent self and you. Counting that just now towards the disrespect count will be waived.]

Shaula: [By the way, what happens when the disrespect count advances~?]

Farsale: [Of course, one of my eminent self's companions will get angry in my stead. If the count were to reach full when it is Reid's turn to get angry, it would be an unimaginable disaster.]

The blonde hair crossed his arms and nodded deeply, but based on Shaula's gut feeling, that disrespect count the one who accumulated it the fastest and the most was probably the red hair, but since the other party looked satisfied, she didn't say it.
Therefore, rewinding the conversation just a little bit,

Shaula: [Did I say something that caught your attention~?]

Farsale: [Other than treating my eminent self like an idiot, did you say something else?]

Shaula: [Just a little before that, your idiocy disappeared, didn't it~. It was then~. Actually, I already forgot what I said, so I can't remember it though~.]

Leaning against the railing set up in the gazebo, Shaula lightly hopped up as if to rest her bottom on it, which was at a position slightly higher than her waist. With that, her eye level became about the same as the blonde hair's.
The blonde hair's red eyes stared directly at Shaula's Scorpion Eyes from the front.

Farsale: […You observe people very closely, do you not?]

Shaula: [――? Anyone would notice if a cloud covered the sun and made a huge shadow~. I thought it was something similar to that, though~.]

Farsale: [Haha, you compare my eminent self to the sun, do you. That will raise your awe points.]

Yet another different point system emerged, but judging from the blonde hair's face, this seemed to be the type of points where accumulating them was not a problem. The deciding factor for acquiring them wasn't reproducible, but since disrespect points meant getting angry in the blonde hair's stead, it might be something like praising in the blonde hair's stead.
In that case, she wanted to aim for “his” timing and actively acquire them.

Farsale: [Shaula, girl who was granted the name of a star. You taught my eminent self before, did you not? That the stars, have the power to grant someone's wish.]

Perhaps it was because her mind was on such things. At the blonde hair's words starting like that, Shaula was briefly dumbfounded, and her reaction was delayed.
After a beat, she immediately recalled that it was about when they gazed at the starry sky together,

Shaula: [Ah~, I said that~. However, the right to have a wish granted is a game of musical chairs… I also taught you the secret to surviving that along with it, didn't I~.]

Farsale: [Right you were, right you were. To shine brightly, so much that even the stars are captivated… Truly, it is such a logical idea that even my eminent self could not help but groan in admiration.]

Shaula: [Heheh, naturally~. After all, I am Master's cute, cute disciple~.]

Rubbing under her nose with her finger, Shaula proudly accepted the praise from the blonde hair. Relaxing his lips at Shaula's reaction, the blonde hair however smoothly withdrew that smile,

Farsale: [If so, to those who were in that place earlier, my eminent self and your Master are not stars in the heavens, but stars upon the earth, I suppose.]

Shaula: [――. Stars upon the, earth~?]

Farsale: [Umu, stars upon the earth. How somewhat embarrassing to call oneself that!]

Letting out a loud voice, the blonde hair laughed cheerfully. However, to Shaula, it felt as though the blonde hair was trying to clear away the fog right before his eyes by letting out a loud voice.
What lay hidden behind the blonde hair's foolishness, Shaula did not know its true identity. Not knowing it, but the blonde hair had spoken just now as something that involved not just himself, but "him" as well.
Stars not in the sky, but on the earth. ――If stars were things that granted someone's wishes.

Shaula: [Farsale, did you get sick of that~?]

Farsale: [――――]

At Shaula's question, the blonde hair before her was caught off guard, his eyes going perfectly round.
That was the very expression of the blonde hair Shaula knew, exposing his foolishness, his natural expression.

Farsale: [Hahaha! Be at ease, Shaula. There is absolutely no way my eminent self feels that role is a burden and wants to run away. Because my eminent self believes this role is my true calling!]

Shaula: [Seriously~? But, if that's the case, why did you bring me out here~. Your actions and words contradict each other… this taste, is the taste of a liar~hk!]

Farsale: [Why did you just lick the back of my eminent self's hand!?]

Having his hand taken by Shaula who smoothly reached out, and moreover, having the back of his hand licked, the blonde hair panicked. As she continued to look at him suspiciously, the blonde hair shrugged his shoulders with a "Good grief",

Farsale: [Listen here, Shaula. You, if I recall correctly, like appas, do you not.]

Shaula: [Well, yeah~. Because Master likes them~.]

Farsale: [But what if you had to eat ten thousand, a hundred thousand, a million appas? Even if it is something you like, you might lose the taste for it.]

Shaula: [Is that so~? If I'm with Master, even if it's a hundred million appas, I think I could eat them freshly, deliciously, and with a smile~.]

Farsale: [Muu, is that so. That means my eminent self underestimated the depth of love between you and your Master… no, if it is a difference in the magnitude of love, does it mean my eminent self still has a long way to go…]

Shaula: [Heee~y, can the conversation return to the original topic~?]

Having a hand fluttered in front of his face, the blonde hair gasped with a "No, no".

Farsale: [Uumu, what my eminent self wanted to say got all jumbled up, but to get straight to the point, what my eminent self wants to say is that in order to like appas tomorrow as well, we humans need to take a breather.]

Shaula: [Haa~, how frail~. To think you need reasons and effort just to keep liking what you like, humans really love to worry, I can't believe it~.]

Farsale: [Ah, looking at you, I cannot help but think so.]

The blonde hair lowered the corners of his eyes like that. Even the blonde hair, who usually looked foolish, was like that. The beard and Mama-sama were like that too, and sometimes even “he” was like that, so humans were busy. As a result, the suspicion of being a monster surfaced again for the red hair, who didn't seem to have any worries despite being a human.
And so, driving thoughts of that red hair out of her head, Shaula said to the blonde hair in front of her,

Shaula: [Can't be helped then~. In that case, I'll show you how it's done~.]

Still resting her bottom on the railing, she said that while resting her cheek on her own thigh.
The blonde hair widened his eyes yet again, looking perplexed with a "You?", but――,

Shaula: [I'm a Scorpio woman who received the name of a star from Master, y'know~? That's why I will teach you guys who lack the capacity to play the star~. The way of a star~.]

Farsale: [――――]

Pointing at herself with her thumb up, the blonde hair was at a loss for words at Shaula, who smiled like that. However, as that loss for words slowly unraveled, a face typical of the blonde hair peeked out from beyond it.
Namely, a foolish smile that wasn't holding anything back.

Farsale: [Is that so… Is that so! You will show us the example! That is such a reliable tale to hear! Truly, splendid!]

Shaula: [Ooh~? Don't carelessly clear the sky in front of the Scorpio woman shining in the starry sky~.]

Farsale: [Indeed! Now that you mention it, it is so! You are truly smart.]

Laughing, her head was patted by the unreservedly reaching hand of the blonde hair, and Shaula pursed her lips.
After giving a wry smile at Shaula's reaction, the blonde hair took a step back and took something out of his pocket.
Seeing that, Shaula let out a voice saying "Ah". ――It was a red, red, glossy appa.

Farsale: [I did not have the leeway to put anything in my mouth at the banquet, you see. I brought just one with me. ――Shall we share this between my eminent self and you?]

Shaula: […Makes no sense~. Aren't you hungry~? With just one appa, your belly won't swell that much~.]

Farsale: [Oh, as you can see, my eminent self is dressed up tonight, so I cannot carelessly swell my belly. However, leaving half-eaten food is also unbearable. Therefore, having you eat half is the best.]

Shaula: [Is that a wish to the stars~? Something like that…]

Farsale: [Something like that?]

The blonde hair tilting his head, from his hand, Shaula swiftly snatched the appa. And, in the blink of an eye, she split that red, round fruit in half right down the middle. Juice dripped, dirtying Shaula's hands. While licking off that sweet juice, Shaula held out one of the split appa halves,

Shaula: [It's too trivial a wish, so even a star felt like granting it in its spare time~.]

