To those who had been “Hyperphagia'd” by Reilani, Reilani was a friend, a mentor, a lover, family, and the most important existence in this world.

Thus, they would not hesitate to offer their lives for Reilani's sake. They would shield her with their bodies from any opponent, throw away their own bodies to serve her, and love her until their souls burned out.

Reilani: [Everyone was a person possessing a generous heart, willing to pity a woman like me.]

The purpose of Reilani coming to the Augria Sand Dunes was the Pleiades Watchtower―― and beyond it, the shrine where the “Witch of Envy” was sealed. She knew that numerous obstacles, difficulties, and hardships would befall her to reach there, but Reilani did not underestimate them.
Because she was the existence most befitting to be pitied in this world, she had no such leeway.

Thus, Reilani gathered one hundred and fifty dragon carriages and nine hundred people who would carefully pity her, and challenged the Augria Sand Dunes. ――The result could be called a disastrous scene.

The nine hundred pity-warriors scattered into the sand one after another, and the one hundred and fifty ground dragons also perished miserably. They desperately threw their lives away to protect Reilani no matter what, but it was in vain.

The cruel Sand Sea swallowed the wisdom of the pity-warriors, and finally, Reilani's life was also hanging by a thread.

In a close call, the most pitiful woman in the world, Reilani Alnair, would have lost her life there――,

Shaula: [Well, it's easier and better if you don't move like that~.]

When she heard that voice and her life was saved, Leilani became certain. ————That toward this woman who ought to be pitied most in the world, even fate felt pity. 

2

The days of Shaula, who styled herself the Watcher of the tower claiming the role of “Star-keeper”, were an accumulation of pain that deserved pity for Reilani.

Possessing hardly any human emotions at all, Shaula did not exhibit a single fragment of mercy such as compassion or consideration, which should be voluntarily given to the pitiable weak. In the humiliating circumstance of indelicately having to ask for consideration herself, Reilani could not help but pity herself.


――However, no matter how foolish an existence Shaula was, she could not escape the effects of “Hyperphagia”.


Surely, slowly but steadily, the carefree Shaula's memories were “Hyperphagia'd” by Reilani, and she knew that the faces, voices, scents, and everything else of the people she had met, liked or disliked, nurtured bonds with, and exchanged love with in her life thus far were repainted into “Reilani”, changing the way she interacted with her.


The trigger for that influence was, without a doubt, the existence of the babies in Reilani's belly.
Reilani's Authority, which was so difficult to use it deserved pity, required a long time to “Hyperphagia” a target. The more “Hyperphagia” progressed, the bigger Reilani's existence inside the other party became, but the target prior to that point did not even feel pity for Reilani.
Thus for Reilani, normally an opponent like Shaula, with whom neither words nor common sense could communicate, was the most dangerous and difficult existence to deal with.


Against such a target, Reilani was nothing more than a pitifully powerless woman. ――That was where it became useful,her greatly swollen belly, in other words, the proof of a pregnant woman.
Strangely enough, people tend to excessively pity the creature known as a pregnant woman.
She was honestly surprised that this logic worked even on that Shaula, but this time as well, Reilani was flawlessly pitied, and she had reached the point of activating the Authority of “Hyperphagia”.

This too was the achievement of Reilani's babies―― babies she had kept in her womb by sheer willpower for over three years in order to constantly be the pitiable existence of a pregnant woman, and seemingly multiple babies at that. However, the crucial babies, as if ignorant of their pitiable mother's hard work, foolishly kicked her belly from the inside time and time again, ceaselessly appealing to be let out.

The babies knew nothing of the feelings of that pitiable mother who had children ignorant of their parent's heart.


In this world, all sorts of unreasonableness and absurdity rained down inescapably. There was no more pitiable event than being born into such a place. As a mother, Reilani truly pitied her children from the bottom of her heart and kept them in her womb.
Pitiably, such prayers of Reilani were completely uncommunicated to the children kicking her belly even now.

Shaula: [Reilani~, chow's ready~. If I taste-test it, your portion will decrease, so do the taste-testing yourself~.]

With a drawling voice, Shaula, who had been boiling a pot for Reilani, called over here.
Unlike in the beginning, Shaula's attitude towards Reilani had softened considerably. In conversations with her, who did not hide her throwaway and blunt attitude and treated her as a nuisance head-on, her nerves were worn out, but the Shaula who treated the pitiable pregnant Reilani harshly was no more.


――“Hyperphagia” had progressed, and the repainting of the majority of Shaula's memories was already complete.

The memories inside her, in almost every single scene “Reilani” was there, and the entrances and exits of every emotion were filled up by “Reilani”. There were probably scenes where multiple “Reilani”s were present at the same time, but Shaula did not notice.

That was not because Shaula was particularly foolish. ――It was not just her, anyone would be like that.
No one could notice the effects of Reilani's “Hyperphagia” Authority. Because no one could ever doubt the precious memories inside themselves.
Much less, they could not suspect that it was brought about by a trivial, pitiable woman.

Shaula: [Reilani~?]

Tilting her head and calling out to her with a completely foolish face, Reilani smiled deeply with pity at Shaula.
Many felt a dark superiority in extending a hand to a pitiable woman. Shaula too could not resist the amusement embraced by numerous people. Captured, bound, and devoured completely.
Using the wreckage of the broken dragon carriage and blankets, Reilani raised herself from the bed Shaula had prepared, and through “Hyperphagia”, pitied Shaula who pitied the pitiable Reilani.
――The “Gospel” instructed Reilani to head to the shrine of the “Witch of Envy”.
Just as all Witch Cultists did, Reilani, the Sin Archbishop of “Gluttony”, also did not harbor the thought of defying the writings in the “Gospel”. The “Gospel” certainly brought good news―― making Reilani, continue to be an existence deserving of pity.


Therefore, in order to comply with the writings of the “Gospel”, Reilani prepared the nine hundred people she had “Hyperphagia'd” and challenged the Sand Sea. Those nine hundred people and one hundred and fifty ground dragons who pitied Reilani had been completely annihilated, but the foolish “Star-keeper” she obtained in their stead should be able to fulfill their role sufficiently.
Devoured completely by “Hyperphagia”, Shaula was no longer dominated by anything but pity for Reilani. Thus――,

Reilani: [――Shaula-sama.]

Shaula: [Nn~? What is it~?]

While remaining seated on the bed, Shaula did not move at Reilani calling out like that. Even though she was appealing for her to quickly show pity and lend a hand since she was a pregnant woman, what an unperceptive idiot.
Without showing a hint of such pity, Reilani gently stroked her swollen belly,

Reilani: [Having been graced with your kind and generous mercy, unworthy me is disproportionately happy. After all, you have considered my incompetent self as your number one priority.]

Shaula: [――Hah? No I didn't~?]

Reilani: [Eh]

――A white light pierced through.

3

Reilani: [――Ah]

Her feet catching on the feel of the sand, she pitched forward and collapsed on the spot. ――She could not take another step. With her willpower and physical strength completely exhausted, Reilani sincerely pitied herself as she simply waited for death.

It was an overly incomprehensible, heinous act.

What was with that relaxed face up until then? Suddenly transforming completely, immediately after, the eyes of Shaula, who pierced Reilani with light, were devoid of emotion.

It wasn't anger, or murderous intent. With eyes that eliminated all emotion, she shot Reilani.
And, taking Reilani, who was on the verge of death from a single blow, outside the tower, she threw her out into the sea of sand.

Reilani: [――Igh]

Gasping for breath, letting the sand absorb the blood flowing profusely from her pierced body, Reilani pitied herself suffering from Shaula's despicable act.

Even after doing all this, Shaula did not deal the finishing blow to Reilani. She threw her out into the sea of sand just like that, but left the luggage containing food and water beside her. However, she neither took Reilani to people nor called for help.

The meaning, she did not understand. ――No, she understood. Understanding it, she pitied herself.

Reilani: [――Ugh]

She wouldn't kill her. She wouldn't let her live either. It was a shameful gamble that left only the final choice to heaven without cruelly dirtying her own hands. ――How pitiable Reilani was.

Reilani: [――Eh]

The flowing blood was exactly Reilani's life force itself. When it ran completely dry, the pitiable Reilani's life would be miserably scattered in the sand. That was also transmitted to the babies inside her swollen womb, who were thrashing about more than usual, trying to kick through her uterus. The babies panicking at their mother's predicament were also aware. That if things continued this way, they would be taken down with her.

Reilani: [――Oh]

Naturally, if Reilani died, the children in her womb would die too. Or rather, they might already be dead. The single strike of light unleashed by Shaula pierced right below Reilani's chest.
There was probably no reason other than it being easy to aim at, but it would be no wonder if that one strike had taken the lives of the multiple fetuses who knew nothing of the outside. If there was a dead child, it would be a pity, but after all, it was only a matter of sooner or later, and it fell far short of Reilani's pitifulness.

After all, to have someone with whom she shared blood so close, yet for them to be nothing more than babies in her womb who couldn't offer any help, could there be anything more pitiable?
As expected, Reilani was the most pitiable in the world――,

Voice: [――Hey! It is a person after all! Someone collapsed! They are still alive!]

Suddenly, the thick, desperate voice of a man struck strongly against the ears of Reilani, who was pitying herself.

The presence of someone rushing over, and the sound of kicking sand. Her body roughly lifted by sturdy arms that had come right beside her, an unfamiliar face reflected in the hazy, blurred vision of Reilani panting in agony.

It wasn't Shaula. A man. That man wasn't alone; there was a presence of several others hurriedly rushing over. Everyone had faces that pitied the woman who had suffered a fatal injury.
At that fact, Reilani felt that fate had pitied her and extended a hand. As expected, it was only natural for even fate to pity the most pitiable woman in the world――,

Man: [It is a terrible wound... besides, are you pregnant? This is bad... she needs treatment!]

The man shouted, throwing out instructions to those around him. Hearing the word "treatment," Reilani realized the man had knowledge of healing magic, and rejoiced at further pity from fate.
In contrast to Reilani's joy, the man grimaced as if lamenting, "Shit!",

Man: [One is already a goner, they're dead...! But, another one... no, two are alive!]

Reilani: [――]

Man: [The babies... no, should we prioritize her...]

In the process of checking the state of the wound, the man who noticed the existence of the children in the womb vocalized his hesitation. From that tone, Reilani immediately sensed that there was no means to save both mother and child. Sensing it, Reilani mustered all her strength and instinctively grabbed the man's arm.
With a "――hk", the man's eyes widened, and while being peered into by those eyes, Reilani made her voice tremble.

Reilani: [B-babies, u...]


At the faltering, broken appeal, the man widened his eyes.
That's right, the babies didn't matter. She couldn't care less about lives not yet born. She wanted him to help the pitiable woman right in front of him today. The pitiable Reilani, who looked like she was about to breathe her last at any moment. Babies, she could make again as long as she, the mother, was around. Originally, she didn't even know who the father was; they were nothing more than the seed of someone who had pitied Reilani, mere accessories to invite pity.
And yet――,

Man: [――! Ah... ah, I understand! Of course! I will properly save them! Yours, your babies will not die!]

In an instant, a mother on the brink of death mustering her love for her children―― yes, misinterpreting Reilani's appeal, a fire of strong resolve lit up in the man's eyes.

Reilani: [Wr...ong, m-me...]

She desperately writhed, trying to correct that mistake. It was useless. Reilani's body, having lost too much blood, wouldn't listen, yet her throat was blocked by overflowing blood, and Reilani's appeal was churned into a gurgling, grating sound, failing to be vocalized correctly. Without being vocalized―― assaulted by intense pain as if her brain was being directly scrambled, Reilani's consciousness was dyed white.

Reilani: [――]

Her belly, was being torn open. The already existing hole in her belly was widened, and the sensation of her internal organs being pushed aside arrived in quick succession, and in exchange for Reilani's life, the babies were dragged out.

At that pain, that sense of loss, that despairing agony, the Sin Archbishop of "Gluttony" screamed.
Stop it stop it stop it stop it [――Aaaaaaaaaah] stop it stop it stop it stop it stop stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it [――Igiiiih] stop it stop it stop it stop it stop stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it [――Ugo, gi, gugehh] stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it [――Ea, eaa, eaa] stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it stop it [――O, oh] stop it stop it stop it stop it――.

Shouting, writhing, crying, screaming, Reilani sought the world's pity.
But, it wouldn't stop. ――The hands of the man trying to see a mother's affection through to the end, wouldn't stop.

Reilani: [――]

Eventually, around the time those screams died down, the first cries of two baby boys born into this world reached the ears of this pitiful woman, whose true feelings were never understood by anyone until her final dying moments. 

Held in the man's arms, the two newborn babies brought into this world were seeing off their dying mother—who was perishing in exchange for their life—while letting out newborn cries as if taking pity on her. ——My children, who were "Gluttony" in its absolute extremity, committing the cardinal sin of killing their mother and devouring her life the moment they were born.
Listening to those newborn cries fading into the distance, Reilani Alnair pitied herself.
——Pitying herself, thinking that, after all, she truly was the most pitiful woman in the world.

Epilogue “Days I Waited for You”

1

Twinkling, twinkling, flickering.
Twinkling, twinkling, shining.
Twinkling, twinkling, dazzling.
Twinkling, twinkling, sparkling, everything was vividly gleaming.

Shaula: [――Nn~, the wake-up smooch from Master is put on hold for today too, huh~.]

Stretching her just-awakened body vigorously, Shaula succeeded in welcoming a crisp awakening all on her own on this day as well.
Cracking her neck bones with a popping sound, she stretched on the spot with an "Uii~".

Shaula: [Ah~, my head's been feeling somewhat fuzzy~ so I've been under a lot of stress for a while~, but at long last [I feel refreshed~. Bottling things up is seriously bad for your health after all~.]

Reflecting on her mental and physical unhealthiness of late, Shaula acutely realized the importance of the foundation of beauty. Originally, thinking about this and that was unsuited for Shaula.
She was designed by Mama-sama in such a way, and even after that, through her associations with the red hair, the blonde hair, and the beard, Shaula had grown up freely like that.
Of course, it went without saying that the most important factor for the large flower named Shaula to bloom was “his” affection.

Shaula: [But, it was a weird feeling~. To mistake Mama-sama for someone else, if the person herself found out, she’d definitely make incredibly sarcastic remarks to me~. Phew, how scary~.]

Moreover, it wasn’t just Mama-sama whom she had misunderstood, but the other red hairs and such as well.
Thinking it might have been a hallucination shown by accumulated fatigue, she had tried sleeping plenty yesterday. As a result, both her hair glossiness and skin glossiness were at their peak, but honestly, the level of crispness in her head was unclear.
At any rate, since she had kicked out the uninvited guest, there wouldn’t be any more misunderstandings like that.

Shaula: [Even so, to try and take my number one… namely, Master’s seat, there is a limit to being endlessly insolent~. That’s a straight red card and ejection~.]

From Shaula’s perspective, she was a woman who made a completely incomprehensible misunderstanding.
She was an opponent whose name was already fuzzy, but no matter how out-of-bounds a statement she made from Shaula’s point of view, there was no mistaking that she was a pregnant woman. Therefore, Shaula made a concession of a straight red card while keeping “his” command as a premise―― an ejection not from this world, but from the tower.

Shaula: [Since I tossed her outside the ‘Sand Time’, and gave her water and food just in case, the rest is a test of luck to see if someone passes by~.]

Honestly, from Shaula’s perspective, she was confident that it was quite a cunning answer that slipped through a loophole in “his” command, but if she were asked whether she could let “him” hear about it, she felt suspicious about it, so she considered it a choice right on the borderline of whether she kept it or not.
Fortunately, the opponent’s slip of the tongue happened in the morning, so tossing her out was during the day when the possibility of people passing by was not entirely zero. If she was saved, the person herself should also be thankful for her own luck.
In any case, the days with the uninvited guest reminded Shaula of the existence of another person for the first time in hundreds of years, but she didn’t gain much from it. It felt cramped, and not for me.

Shaula: [Ah, but there was just one thing I wanted to thank her for~.]

Because of that, perhaps she had thought to save that foreigner’s life, other than the pretext of half-keeping “his” command.
That was――,

Shaula: [――I was able to reaffirm that after all, only Master can fill the hole left by Master, so I thanked her just for that part~.]

――That was the harvest from the few days Shaula spent with the uninvited foreigner.

2

Twinkling, twinkling, flickering.
Twinkling, twinkling, shining.
Twinkling, twinkling, dazzling.
Twinkling, twinkling, sparkling, everything was vividly gleaming.

Shaula: [――Nn~, today as well, the wake-up back hug from Master has vanished like dew~.]

The days since then, for Shaula, were the arrival and departure of unchanging everydays, which were repeated and piled up over and over again.
The sun rose, set, rose again, and set again repeatedly, and amidst that, Shaula continued to gaze at the unchanging sea of sand while performing her fixed routine.

Shaula: [――O~ne two~, three, four~!]

Conceived by “him”, Mama-sama giving up before even doing ten percent, the beard awkwardly keeping company, the blonde hair accomplishing it while laughing heartily, and the red hair giving a big yawn and paying no attention.

Performing such a memorable radio calisthenics, Shaula bathed her entire body in the sunlight.
Because “he” had taught her that it was necessary to maintain a glamorous nice body.

Shaula: [――With this feeling, just keeping it closed might be suspicious~.]

While muttering so somewhat apologetically, Shaula looked around the stone room carved with countless ‘tally marks’, snapped her fingers, and produced the gunports for Hell’s Snipe―― something that was once said she would be full-fledged if she could produce ten of, producing over a hundred at once, and aimed them at the walls.

And then, the stone room that was guaranteed to make “him” completely creeped out when he returned, she forcefully remodeled―― against the rule forbidding the destruction of the tower, sticking her tongue out with a “I’m not a challenger~.”

Shaula: [――Come to think of it, if I had kept some appa seeds, could they have been grown in the green room, I wonder~.]

Suddenly voicing such an idea, Shaula regretted a rather old event.
The only other existence in the tower besides Shaula to have spent a long time, the Spirit of the green room―― she had no sense of camaraderie with it as it didn’t even show its form, but if nature were to somehow grow inside the tower, it would only be there.

However, even within the tower, only that place was the territory of the green room―― having done things with such a tacit understanding all this time, it seemed adding a hand to it by Shaula would be frowned upon. Well, if it was seriously in the way it would be war, but although they had almost no interaction, their association was long. She let it slide~.

Shaula: [――Could it be that the pack changed generations~? Trying to challenge me, you’re seriously idiots~.]

While procuring food, she went down to the ground and was shooting Witchbeasts dead left and right, when a grotesque Witchbeast that was half-human, half-horse―― a Hungry Horse King attacked in a pack, and she annihilated them.
The previous pack, by making an example of the top of the pack, had stopped laying a hand on Shaula since then, but as generation changes progressed, the effect of making an example faded.
With no other choice, she blasted them with Hell’s Snipe, making them understand the difference in power. If she didn’t do so, the Witchbeasts would try to enter the tower as well, so the Star-keeper’s job was busy.

Shaula: [――I’m seriously too admirable & cute~. Master should be aware that he’s letting go of an extraordinary opportunity loss and the affection dividends he ought to be receiving~.]

Every single day, day in and day out, a mind and body polished for “his” sake, the obedience of continuing to protect “his” command, the endless affection that grew thinking of “him”―― she wanted “him” to properly understand that none of these were things to be taken for granted.

Shaula: [――Nah, he doesn’t have to understand it~. Even if he doesn’t understand, I’ll just report it directly to Master from my own mouth, and have him understand it~.]

Therefore, even a day, even a second sooner, even if just for a single glance,

Shaula: [――I want to see you~, Master.]

3

Twinkling, twinkling, flickering.
Twinkling, twinkling, shining.
Twinkling, twinkling, dazzling.
Twinkling, twinkling, sparkling, everything was vividly gleaming.

――The arrival of that day was without any warning, a sudden occurrence.

That dragon carriage was a challenger that had broken through the ‘Sand Time’ and charged into this side after a long time.
However, even if they could break through the ‘Sand Time’, waiting ahead was a Witchbeast zone that was a field of flowers where countless Courtesan Bears grew in clusters. In most cases―― or rather, almost certainly, it was a given that those who cleared the primary exam of the ‘Sand Time’ would fall to the secondary exam of the fierce assault of the Witchbeasts.
But, these challengers, without making the common foolish mistake of waking the sleeping pack of Courtesan Bears, calmly detoured around the flower field, vividly showing their difference from the others.

Shaula: […hk]


At that brilliant handling, she understood that heat rippled across the vast ocean of Shaula’s heart.
If they could respond so accurately to the baptism of the Augria Sand Dunes, perhaps that was the return of “him” that Shaula had been eagerly waiting for.
However, even that expectation, due to the challengers taking their time to have a leisurely discussion after leaving the Witchbeast zone, deflated with tremendous momentum.

Shaula: [Here’s a boom~.]

Towards the group that was perfectly caught in her sights, Shaula blasted a Hell’s Snipe.
Her attitude in releasing it was careless, proportional to the heat of expectation that had been raised just before. But, to defend herself, it was the fault of the challengers who betrayed her expectation. That was all, defense concluded.

Shaula: [If it was Master――]

If the one who had returned was “him”, he should have waved his hand, raised a smoke signal, or given some kind of sign towards Shaula, whom he had left behind in the tower as the ‘Star-keeper’.
If there was a sign, no matter how unfamiliar it was to Shaula, she was more than mentally prepared to ad-lib and play along.
However, there was no sign. ――Then, it was not “him”.
Shaula had zero hesitation in trying to blow away their lives with Hell’s Snipe.
However――,

Shaula: [――Oh? Seriously~? They defended against it~.]


Noticing Shaula’s Hell’s Snipe, an ice wall was instantly put up in multiple layers.
Of course, Hell’s Snipe was not an ultimate technique that could be stopped by that level of thing, but having its power and speed slightly slowed down by the ice wall, a single sword from someone in the group slashed it down.

If she had still been inexperienced it would be one thing, but having her Hell’s Snipe, refined over hundreds of years, stopped was a first in Shaula’s history. At that rare experience, her once deflated sense of expectation breathed just a little bit of life again, and Shaula opened the next gunport.
She didn’t think it was “him”, but it might be a challenger who cleared the conditions “he” imposed and possessed the qualifications to enter the tower. In order to confirm that, she immediately blasted a second shot.

And that was defended against in a strange way different from before――,

Shaula: [――Eh?]

In that instant, with a sense of expectation, Shaula, who had narrowed her aim even further, doubted her eyes.

Shaula: [No way… can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be, can’t be~hk…]

Inside a strange magical field, right in the dead center of the scene where Hell’s Snipe had been attenuated, Shaula caught sight of an impossible opponent―― no, not impossible. Not, impossible.
There was no way it could be impossible. Because, “he”, had promised Shaula――.
That he would definitely return, so wait for him, yes, because he had promised――.

Shaula: [――Found you.]

――At a perilous moment, in the nick of time, Shaula had made it in time.
The mana pool that was the cause of the ‘Sand Time’ was unraveled by “his” magic, and as a result, “he”, along with those who were with him, fell to the bottom of the Sand Sea. Shaula headed to recover them in a great panic, but missed the two choices of “him” and the others who had split into two groups, swinging and missing once. Shoving the confusing bunch into the tower, she headed for the other choice―― and there, “he” was on the verge of death.

Shaula: […Or something, maybe you didn’t even need my help~?]

Facing a single Hungry Horse King that had strayed from its pack, “he” was engaged in a mortal combat.
Of course, since it was the immortal and invincible “him”, Shaula’s help was probably unnecessary. But it couldn’t be helped. She wanted to show off her cool side. She wanted him to see that while “he” didn’t know, she had become this strong, that “his” student had protected his commands.
She wanted him to see, and then, and then, she wanted him to praise her.

Shaula: [Master, I, worked super hard~. I, wanted to be super praised~.]

The moment of reunion, it was frustratingly postponed.
Going limp and losing consciousness, sleeping while hugging an unknown woman, “his” unchanging lack of principles made her go “Grrr~”, but it was a law of nature for capable men to be popular.

Besides――,

Shaula: [Right now, I’m seriously over the moon with joy and happiness, so I can overlook most things with the spirit of a goddess of mercy~. Really, truly, this isn’t a dream, right~?]

Pinching her own cheek with a finger, Shaula confirmed the dream she wouldn’t wake up from, and felt relieved.
The moment she felt relieved, scarlet immediately rose to her cheeks, and her eyes grew moist. The beating of her heart became loud, and she couldn’t stay still on the spot.

Shaula: [Master, Master, Master, Master, Master…]

With every word she uttered, she knew her chest grew hot, her cheeks broke into a grin, and her heart melted sweetly.
Even though she had been eagerly waiting for this day for so, so long, when that day actually arrived, she couldn’t even organize the order of the things she had only been thinking she wanted to do and say.

Shaula: [Ah~, but, but, there’s no mistaking just this, so this is the very first of the first~.]

Even if her emotions were congested, her feelings were crossed, and her thoughts became incoherent, just this was absolute.
Through the days she continued to wait, only this feeling of the Scorpio woman was an absolute genuine thing that would never waver――.

Twinkling, twinkling, flickering, shining, dazzling, you who vividly gleamed.

Shaula: [――No matter if hundreds of years pass, I’ve alwa~ys loved you~, Master.]

