Hey everyone! Thank you so much for coming along for the ride with another Blu-ray/DVD bonus novel!

It feels like I was just writing the bonus novel for Season 3 a moment ago, but thankfully, I’ve been given the chance to write one for Season 4 as well. Ah, right—when the gap between anime seasons is short, the deadline for the next bonus novel comes around that much faster. Quite the blind spot. Well, I had a blast writing it though!

At any rate, this story put the spotlight front and center on Shaula—a key character who makes her debut and plays a major role in Season 4!

It’s essentially a memoir of the endless time she spent as the Star Keeper in the Pleiades Watchtower before Subaru’s group arrived, forcibly exposed by an unexpected visitor. As keen readers have likely figured out, Reilani Alnair—who appeared here—was the previous Sin Archbishop of Gluttony, making her the "predecessor" to the current Gluttony siblings. While you’ll have to fill in some of the finer details with your imagination, this story reveals the hidden history connecting them.

By the way, since this bonus novel comes with Volume 1 of the Season 4 anime, I imagine anime-only fans were left going, "Wait, what’s happening?!" But don't worry! Everyone who reads the original web/light novels was going "Wait, what’s happening?!" too. That’s just how packed with never-before-revealed lore this rare little volume was.

Four hundred years ago, the companions who endured those days alongside Shaula, a glimpse into the global politics surrounding them, the chaotic adventures of a party traveling through a Re:Zero world very different from today's, and the world-altering changes they brought about that lead into the present—all of it is a sneak peek at stories that will eventually be told.

While those events will be depicted from a different perspective in the main story down the line, for now, SCORPION TALE comes to a close after proving the enduring power of Shaula’s love, undimmed even after hundreds of years. As for the moment the person she so deeply longed to meet finally arrived, and just how overwhelmed with joy she was—I'll leave that depiction for the main story itself.

As I write this afterword, the anime broadcast hasn't quite reached the point where it portrays the depth of Shaula’s emotions yet, but I have no doubt it’s going to be absolute perfection.

Look forward to the ending that awaits Shaula’s four hundred years of solitude!

Once again, thank you from the bottom of my heart for reading this bonus novel to the very end! I’ll keep pouring my soul into every single word so you can enjoy Re:Zero to its absolute fullest, so please keep supporting the series moving forward!

Alright then, Season 4 has one more bonus novel lined up, so I’m gonna go put my back into writing that one too!

The anime turned out amazing, so be sure to rewatch and savor it a few hundred times! See you next time!!

(As I stare enraptured at the brand-new illustrations for the Blu-ray/DVD)



